# Patterns here are anchored at the build context (Backend/). Without `**/` a
# pattern matches the top level only: `__pycache__` and `*.log` used to exclude
# nothing below Backend/ itself.

.venv
venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov

reports
**/*.log
logs

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Tenant and local data that is gitignored but sits in a working copy, so a
# `docker compose build` on the deployment host baked it into the image: 125
# compliance evidence uploads, local SQLite databases and the vulnerability
# feed staging area were all in the build context (measured 24 Sep 2026). None
# of it is tracked, so a CI checkout never has it; these lines make the image
# the same wherever it is built. Tracked data under data/ — compliance seeds,
# benchmarks, wordlists, manuf.txt — is unaffected.
data/compliance_evidence
data/feeds
**/*.db

.git
.gitignore
Dockerfile
README.md
